From 72cbfc7bb83f12851838fb55dae0f0379e830977 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angular Dev <dev@medpath.local>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 17:56:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(filters/pagination): repair broken filter, wire real
 pagination, add column sorting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Audited every page for filter/pagination/table bugs.

Bugs fixed:
- Patient History: the search box was two-way bound to a plain
  ('') property inside a computed() — computed() only reacts to
  signal reads, so it had zero tracked dependencies and the
  filtered list never updated after the first render. Typing in
  the box silently did nothing. Converted searchQ to a signal,
  switched the input off ngModel to [value]/(input), added a
  clear (x) button, dropped the now-unused FormsModule import.
- Reports: the pagination footer was fully static markup —
  'Showing 1 to N of N', a hardcoded page '1', and permanently
  disabled prev/next buttons — so it never did anything even
  though the page already had more rows than fit. Replaced it
  with real client-side pagination (5/page): working prev/next,
  numbered page buttons, correct 'Showing X-Y of Z', and the
  range auto-clamps if a filter shrinks the result set below the
  current page. Also wired up the 'Filter reports' icon button,
  which had no click handler at all, into a working All / Pending
  / Dispatched status filter — combined with search, and both
  reset back to page 1 on change.

New: shared/utils/table-sort.ts — a small generic TableSort<T>
helper (click-to-sort, asc/desc toggle, numeric-aware compare,
optional per-column accessors for derived/formatted values like
currency strings) plus a shared .th-sort header style in
styles.css so any table can adopt it without per-page CSS.

Sorting added to every real data table in the app:
- Analytics — 'Top tests ordered' (test, orders, revenue, change)
  and 'Top referring doctors' (doctor, referrals, revenue,
  change); revenue sorts by numeric amount, not the '₹4,750'
  string.
- Sample Tracking — sample queue (ID, patient, priority, status,
  ETA); priority/status sort by clinical urgency rank (STAT/
  critical first) rather than alphabetically. Tube(s) and Tests
  ordered columns are left unsortable since they're multi-value.

Not touched: report-preview / result-entry / print-style report
tables — these render one patient's fixed lab panel in a set
clinical order, not a sortable list, so sorting them would be
wrong. features/dashboard (crypto ticker) isn't wired into any
route — confirmed dead scaffold code, left alone.
